        "description": "<div id=\"link_wrapped_content\">\n<body><section class=\"wp-block-bigbite-multi-title\"><div class=\"container\"></div></section>\n\n\n\n<p>I love standing desks, both as general utility items and as an aid for my bad back. I\u2019ve been using them for a long time, mounting my hefty desktop PC to the bottom to save space and cable routing issues. Lian Li has tempted me with its desk-PC case combos for a while, and never more so than with its stylish new wooden model. There\u2019s just one issue that\u2019s stopping me from buying it.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>The <a href=\"https://lian-li.com/product/dk-07-wood/\">DK-07 WOOD</a> (that\u2019s the name) is a beefy sucker, 1480mm wide (58.26 inches) with support for up to 100 kilograms (220 pounds) on its surface. Inside you\u2019ve got room for two separate E-ATX PC builds, both visible through the stylish glass top, and now upgraded with a riser mount to show off your GPU. There are tons of options for cooling and drive mounts, removable motherboard trays for easy building, storage cubb",
